            <ArticleTitle>[Diagnostic image (93). A boy with a painful leg swelling. Osteoid osteoma].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1179</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 13-year-old boy presented with a swelling on his left lower leg and suffered from pain, which was almost immediately relieved by acetylsalicylic acid. Roentgenographic and histologic appearance demonstrated an osteoid osteoma in the tibia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
